      "name": "sentiment_label",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.7,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "A 3-way sentiment axis is a useful grouping dimension for 'what's worth attention.' Values are mostly sound readings; the Robitussin/'medicinal' review is a defensible negative-lean though arguably neutral. Generally grounded."
    },
    {
      "name": "helpfulness_ratio",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.75,
      "source_groundedness": 0.95,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Directly derived from existing HelpfulnessNumerator/Denominator; NULL for zero-denominator rows is correct behaviour. Gives a real axis to surface reviews the community found useful, though it is largely a deterministic transform of existing columns."
    },
    {
      "name": "review_length_bucket",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.3,
      "source_groundedness": 0.95,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Bucketed text length is grounded and correctly computed, but length is a generic, low-leverage feature for understanding what's actionable in reviews. Adds little analytical value for THIS query."
    },
    {
      "name": "issue_flags",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.55,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "A multi-label topic axis (taste/quality/shipping/value/health/repeat_buy) is highly useful for triaging actionable issues. However groundedness is shaky: the taffy review tagged 'shipping|value|taste' is defensible, but the dog-food review lacks any explicit taste complaint yet gets 'taste'; 'taste' appears near-universally, suggesting an over-broad/default assignment rather than evidence-based extraction."
    },
    {
      "name": "repeat_buy_signal",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.65,
      "source_groundedness": 0.6,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "A repeat-purchase/loyalty flag is analytically valuable for retention insight. Grounding is mixed: the C.S. Lewis confection review is flagged 1 with no clear repeat-buy statement, while the dog-food review ('bought several') is flagged 0 despite explicit repeat purchase — indicating inconsistent, sometimes unsupported inference."
    },
    {
      "name": "exclamation_count",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.2,
      "source_groundedness": 0.95,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Exactly the kind of generic surface-text statistic the query does not need; low analytical leverage. Values are directly countable and grounded."
    },
    {
      "name": "caps_ratio",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.2,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Raw capitalization ratio is a generic text feature with little analytical bearing on what's actionable. Computable from text and grounded, but near-noise for this query."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.5,
  "source_groundedness": 0.75,
  "rationale": "The set mixes genuinely useful analytical axes (issue_flags topic tags, sentiment, helpfulness_ratio, repeat_buy_signal) that give real grouping/triage leverage for surfacing actionable reviews, with several low-value generic surface statistics (review_length_bucket, exclamation_count, caps_ratio) that add little for this query. On groundedness, deterministic transforms are solid, but the inferential columns (issue_flags, repeat_buy_signal) show unsupported or contradictory assignments in the samples — notably a near-ubiquitous 'taste' flag and repeat-buy calls that invert the actual text evidence — dragging overall groundedness below the deterministic columns."
}
